+ readingText:"Last summer, my cousin Ayaan and I travelled by bus from Hargeisa to Berbera. We wanted to spend two days by the sea. The journey usually takes about three hours, but that day was different. We were driving through the hills when the bus suddenly stopped. One of the tyres had a hole. While the driver was changing the tyre, the passengers waited by the road. It was very hot, and we didn't have much water. Then a local family invited us to sit under their tree. They gave us tea and bread. When we finally arrived in Berbera, it was dark, and our hotel had already closed its restaurant. We were tired and hungry, but we weren't angry. Now I pack extra water and some food before every trip. The delay taught me that a problem can also bring a kind surprise.",
